nd learning!\n\n***\n\nCome ready to move, meet new people, and improve your game one rally at a time. We look forward to seeing you on the court!","startDate":"2026-10-08T17:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"NEW TIME!! FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316614280/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-08T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AWS 101 Workshop - Date TBD","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-seneca-polytechnic-newnham-campus/events/316658151/","description":"Welcome to the event where you stop watching and start building.\n\nAWS 101 is our first hands-on workshop, you're setting up your AWS account, getting into the console, and deploying an actual website to a live server before you leave the room. Not a simulation. Not a tutorial you follow at home. Something real, running on AWS infrastructure, with a URL you can send to people.\n\nWe'll walk through the core services that show up in almost every real architecture, (EC2, S3, IAM, RDS) breaking down not just what they are but why they exist and when you'd actually reach for one over another. That thinking is what separates someone who watched a YouTube video from someone who can answer an interview question.\n\nThen we put it all together. Teams of 2-3, a base project already set up, and a challenge to extend it with add-ons wire the database, upgrade the design, add a second page, set up a custom domain. First team to complete all four wins.\n\n**What to expect:**\nA Kahoot to kick off the hands-on section, a live guided build where everyone follows along, a team challenge with actual stakes, and a room full of people figuring things out together.\n**And yes — merch is dropping.** AWS SBG gear will be at this event for the first time. Winners of the challenge get first pick.\n\nFood's covered. Bring your laptop. Set up your AWS Free tier account now.\n\n**DATE TBD, expected early Octobe**r **· Helix Room, K Building, Newnham Campus**","startDate":"2026-10-08T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"1750 Finch Avenue East","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1750 Finch Ave E, North York, ON M2J 5G3, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AWS SBG at Seneca Polytechnic - Newnham Campus","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-seneca-polytechnic-newnham-campus/"},"performer":"AWS SBG at Seneca Polytechnic - Newnham Campus"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Return of the Moral State: Philosophy and the Good Life","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316761865/","description":"Across the world, politics is returning to one of its oldest questions: should the state promote particular, substantive conceptions of the good life? Modern liberalism has approached this ambition with suspicion, seeking instead to leave individuals and communities free to pursue different visions of human flourishing. Yet from Hungary and the United States to China, India, and Israel, influential movements and governments increasingly reject this restraint, using law, education, welfare, media, and public culture to promote specific ideals of family, order, harmony, pride, sacrifice, and belonging.\n\nThis talk examines the return of what I call the “good life state.” I argue that these projects cannot be understood only through the languages of authoritarianism, populism, or democratic backsliding. They also offer substantive moral visions — sometimes attractive, sometimes dangerous — of how people ought to live. Their rise poses a difficult question for liberalism: how can it respond to rival visions of the good life without becoming a good life state itself?\n\nAlexandre Lefebvre\nhttps://profiles.sydney.edu.au/alex.lefebvre\nProfessor of Politics and Philosophy\nUniversity of Sydney\n\n**About the Speaker:**\n\nI’m Professor of Politics and Philosophy at the University of Sydney, where I explore how political ideas shape our lives. Originally from Vancouver, Canada, I earned my PhD at Johns Hopkins University in 2007 and now call Sydney home. For more than a decade, my work has explored one central idea: politics does not just govern us. Political ideas and institutions reach deep into our lives, forming who we are, what we value, and how we understand what makes a life worth living.\n\nMy latest book, **[Liberalism as a Way of Life](https://www.alexlefebvre.com/books)**, argues that liberalism deeply informs not just our politics, but also our values, humor, morality, and so much more. It was named a Best Book of 2024 by The New Yorker, Australian Book Review, Persuasion, and The Ministry of Pop Culture, and was praised as “stirring and clarifying” by David Brooks in *The New York Times* and “daring and engrossing” by Becca Rothfeld in *The Washington Post*.\n\nMy current project, *The Good Life State,* examines a global return to one of politics’ oldest ambitions: using state power to shape citizens’ conceptions of the good life.\n\n**\\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\***\n\nThis is a talk with audience Q&A presented by the University of Toronto's Centre for Ethics that is free to attend and open to the public. Free refreshments will be provided at the event. The talk will also be streamed online with live chat here [to be posted].\n\nAbout the Centre for Ethics (http://ethics.utoronto.ca):\n\nThe Centre for Ethics is an interdisciplinary centre aimed at advancing research and teaching in the field of ethics, broadly defined. The Centre seeks to bring together the theoretical and practical knowledge of diverse scholars, students, public servants and social leaders in order to increase understanding of the ethical dimensions of individual, social, and political life.\n\nIn pursuit of its interdisciplinary mission, the Centre fosters lines of inquiry such as (1) foundations of ethics, which encompasses the history of ethics and core concepts in the philosophical study of ethics; (2) ethics in action, which relates theory to practice in key domains of social life, including bioethics, business ethics, and ethics in the public sphere; and (3) ethics in translation, which draws upon the rich multiculturalism of the City of Toronto and addresses the ethics of multicultural societies, ethical discourse across religious and cultural boundaries, and the ethics of international society.\n\nThe Ethics of A.I. Lab at the Centre For Ethics recently appeared on a list of 10 organizations leading the way in ethical A.I.: https://ocean.sagepub.com/blog/10-organizations-leading-the-way-in-ethical-ai","startDate":"2026-10-08T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Larkin Building, Room 200","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"15 Devonshire Place, University of Toronto, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316616388/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $15 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-08T20:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ROTMAN Author Talk:  Power of Situations","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/314974584/","description":"We attend various ROTMAN events each year. Author Talks. Book Releases. Visiting Professors.\n\n### **Agenda:**\n\n5:00 pm - Check-in opens + light refreshments\n5:30 pm - Author presentation and moderated Q&A\n6:30 pm - Meet-and-greet with author + book signing\n\n### **Book Synopsis:**\n\n**From the #1 bestselling author of *Grit,* a new book that reveals the hidden power of situations—and how you can shape them to bring out your best.**\n\nAngela Duckworth, PhD, is the bestselling author of *Grit* and the founder and CEO of Character Lab. A 2013 MacArthur Fellow, she is a professor of psychology at the University of Pennsylvania.\n\n**In Angela Duckworth’s first book, she showed that a common denominator of successful strivers is a blend of passion and perseverance she dubbed “grit.**”\n\nTicket link is below. $22-$45\n\nThis second book springs from her deepening realization that grit, while necessary, is sometimes not sufficient. How you situate yourself to meet a challenge can be crucial.\nDuckworth’s in-depth research reveals the enormous influence wielded by the objects within arm’s reach, your peers and mentors, and even your zip code. Though you’re often told to make the best of your situation, it is far, far better to make your situation better first.\n\n**In *Situated*, you’ll discover:**\n\n* Why your personality changes, sometimes dramatically, from one situation to another—and how you can harness that shift\n* The secret to conquering temptation *without* willpower\n* Why taking the less effortful path can feel like cheating but often solves a stubborn problem\n* How the company you keep shapes the person you become\n* The most effective ways to help others succeed\n\n***TICKET Link here-***-\n\nhttps://www.rotman.utoronto.ca/news-events-and-ideas/public-events/events-listings/2026/october-2026/oct-8---angela-duckworth/","startDate":"2026-10-08T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"UofT Rotman School of Management","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"105 St George, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/"},"performer":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free English Classes  - in-person at our Toronto school ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/events/316616305/","description":"Practise your English in a friendly, welcoming class in Toronto.\nJoin our free in-person English class and improve your speaking, fluency, grammar and vocabulary with supportive teachers. This class is a great opportunity to practise English, build confidence and meet new people.\n\n**When**\nEvery weekday Monday - Friday\n2.00pm–4.00pm\n\n**Where**\nTeaching House Toronto\nOHC / Sol Camps\n469 Jarvis St\nToronto, ON M4Y 2G8\nCanada\n\n[REGISTER NOW](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)\n\n**What you’ll practise**\n\n* Speaking and fluency\n* Grammar and vocabulary\n* Listening and pronunciation\n* Everyday English for real-life situations\n* Confidence using English with other people\n\n**Who can join?**\nAdults aged 18+ who want to improve their English. Refugees, asylum seekers and newcomers are very welcome.\n\n**About the classes**\nThe classes are taught by trainee English teachers on a Cambridge-accredited CELTA course and supervised by experienced teacher trainers.\n\n**Cost**\nFree\n\n**Before the class**\nPlease arrive a little early so we can welcome you and check your English level.\nSpaces may be limited, so please RSVP if you would like to attend.Cost: FREE\n\nSign up using this [registration form ](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)for automatic reminders and to be on our list for future classes.","startDate":"2026-10-08T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Teaching House Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"469 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/"},"performer":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Drop-In Pickleball (2.5+) – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316616562/","description":"**Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\nCome play one of the fastest-growing sports in North America — right in the heart of the Annex!\nJoin us for friendly, active Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC, just steps from Spadina Station. It’s a great way to stay active, meet new people, and have some fun!\n\n***\n\n**🏓 Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Stop by security and check in at the front desk when you arrive.\n\n***\n\n**🏓 Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\n**RSVP on Meetup does *not* reserve your spot.**\nTo participate in Drop-In Play, you must register and pay in advance via our registration system.\n👉 [Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=xoP7Prl)\n📞 Or register by phone: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\nSpace is limited to **18 players** on a first-come, first-served basis. Once full, no additional participants can be accommodated.\n\n***\n\n**🏓 Other Info:**\n\n* Paddles and balls are available for loan at the front desk with a **$20 cash deposit and valid ID**\n* This session is intended for **novice players and above** — participants should know basic rules and scoring\n* Courts are rotated regularly so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Welcoming, inclusive environment\n\n***\n\nCome ready to rally, socialize, and have a great time on the court. We can’t wait to see you there!","startDate":"2026-10-08T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cafe Français au Black Pony - $3","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/events/316687657/","description":"(English below) Venez profiter de la bonne nourriture et d'une bonne conversation en français au café **Black Pony** situé au **1481 Gerrard St East.** Nous serons à l'arrière du café autour d'une grande table, prêts à vous accueillir.\n\nOn va pratiquer la langue de Molière tout en nous faisant de nouveaux amis(es)s. **Toutes les 30 minutes, nous changerons de place** pour favoriser les échanges. Tout le monde est bienvenu, quel que soit son niveau.\n\nPour en savoir plus sur le café et son menu délicieux et varié : [https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/](https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/)\n\nSi vous ne souhaitez pas que votre photo soit publiée sur MeetUp, veuillez en informer Vishnu.\n\n**Pourquoi ces frais de 3$?** C'est pour payer le coût de l'hébergement sur la plate-forme Meetup pour l’année courante et les années précédentes. Nous vous demandons de payer $3.00 à chaque événement. Vishnu sera là pour recueillir vos contributions. Nous vous prions de bien vouloir apporter de la monnaie.\n\nSi vous préférez, vous pouvez utiliser ce lien pour payer sur Square: [CLIQUER ICI](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nMerci,\n**Vishnu**\n\n..................................................................................................................\n\nCome and enjoy good food and good conversation at the **Black Pony café** located at **1481 Gerrard St East.** We'll be in the back of the café around a big table, ready to welcome you.\n\nWe'll be practicing the French language and making friends, **keeping in mind that every 45 minutes we'll be moving around to mix up the conversation.** Everyone is welcome, whatever your level.\n\nTo find out more about the cafe and its delicious and varied menu: https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/\n\nWhy the $3 fee? It helps cover the cost of hosting the group on the Meetup platform for the current year and previous years. We ask participants to contribute **$3.00 at each event**. Vishnu will be there to collect contributions, so please bring change.\n\nIf you prefer, you can use this Square link:\n[CLICK HERE](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nThank you,\nVishnu","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Black Pony Café and Snack Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1481 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Board Game Night!!!!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/events/316231708/","description":"Hello Meeples!!!!\n\nI host board game night every Thursday at Face to Face Games, located at 1398 Danforth Ave (about a 3 min walk from Greenwood station, or a 7 min walk from Coxwell station)! How it works I’ll be seated at the table at the very back right hand corner of Face to Face Games (near the washrooms).\n\nWe usually have 2 tables reserved for our group. (If you can’t find us, ask one of the staff members.) I’ll bring a variety of games from my own collection to board game night, but attendees are free to bring any of their own games as well! Got a brand new game you’ve been dying to play but never have enough players? Bring it along!\n\nGot a retro game that you think is a hidden gem? Bring it along and spread the joy! I usually come early at around 4:30pm. If there are other attendees who also arrive early, then we can play some shorter games until 6pm. Six o’clock is when the event officially starts and is when most attendees start trickling in.\n\nOnce we have most people assembled, we collectively decide which games we want to play and split into groups accordingly. We usually have one group tackling a heavy board game (ie. a game that tends to be more complex and takes longer to finish) while the others play short to medium-length games, but this is very flexible and will depend on turnout and the kinds of games people bring.\n\nIf you can only get here later or if you arrive late, don’t fret. We’ll see what game you can join so that you can get playing as soon as possible!\n\nRules of the Tables:\n\nWe are a cool and relaxed group - we swear! But to ensure things run smoothly and that everyone is having fun, we do some some rules we would like attendees to follow:\n\n\\- Please be respectful of people’s games and property\\. For example\\, if you’re having a snack \\(please share\\!\\)\\, make sure your fingers are clean before you handle cards\\, mats\\, meeples\\, and the like\\. People are generous to bring their games to board game night\\, so we want to be mindful not to damage or dirty their stuff\\.\n\n\\- Please be mindful of your cellphone usage during the game\\. Of course this doesn’t mean you can’t use your cellphone to shoot a quick text message or to check something quickly\\. we’re not monsters\\!\n\n\\- However\\, if you’re always focused on your cellphone \\(for example\\, watching a video or playing a cellphone game\\) and are not paying attention to the rules being explained\\, or you constantly need the other players to repeat themselves as to what sick moves they just made\\, then it ends up taking away from everyone’s enjoyment of the game\\.\n\n\\- Please be decent\\, in dress and in conduct\\. No bullying\\, excessive swearing\\, racist or sexist language\\, and all the other bad stuff\\.","startDate":"2026-10-08T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Geekz United","url":"https://www.meetup.com/geekzunited/"},"performer":"Geekz United"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/3/c/9/highres_528093737.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/3/4/b/highres_529374091.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/a/8/d/highres_533706797.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/e/0/highres_536283040.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/a/b/0/highres_536375504.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/b/b/d/highres_533707101.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/a/3/highres_451449891.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/5/a/9/highres_534309641.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><meta name="next_csrf" content="6df2d9a0-6dd5-4c96-97df-0ed3e8c0eef0"/><script>(function(){try{if(typeof performance==="undefined"||!performance.getEntriesByType)return;var n=performance.getEntriesByType("navigation");if(!n||!n[0]||!n[